WEBVTT

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:44.920
Yeah! All right!

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.020
Do your best! Go for it!

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.080
It's almost time to change, Kawase.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:49.930
Yes sir!

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.110
Strike!

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.220
Hey, hey.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.690
It's different from what we heard.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:08.320
Kawase Ryoko. I thought she was a female player that just wanted to play,

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.660
but she's incredible.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.240
The speed isn't as great as the guys',

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.620
but if she uses the corners that well, it's hard to hit.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.520
Strike! Batter out!

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.210
Yaginuma! You're the only one who's hitting the balls properly. I'm counting on you!

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.130
Yes sir.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.890
Foul!

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.360
<i>Aiming only for the outer corner, huh?</i>

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.040
<i>Yes, her control is really good,</i>

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.810
<i>but she's underestimating me if she's trying to strike me out with just fastballs.</i>

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.110
<i>I've got it!</i>

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.650
<i>A slider?</i>

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.840
Strike! Batter out!

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.820
<i>I won't lose either, Goro-kun.</i>

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.780
Shigeno Goro. Former name: Honda Goro.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.360
Height: 180cm.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.320
Weight: 75kg.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.230
A third-year on Seishuu Private High School's baseball team.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.540
Pitches left. Hits right.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.890
He broke his right shoulder once and gave up baseball.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.780
But with his unbelievable baseball senses and determination, he switched to southpaw and came back.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.420
After he got into Kaido, a famous school,

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.560
he quit and joined Seishuu, a no-name school.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.480
With a baseball team he built from scratch,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.650
they played their third game yesterday, and the result...

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.440
is exactly what the sports newspapers today are talking about.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.940
With this, I'm sure the other teams will try to scout him.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.870
But we have a connection; an OB,
his father, Shigeno Hideki, is on our side.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.900
Even if we can't change the fact that Mayumura is our first choice,

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.110
we should think about getting this player on our team-

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.060
Wait a moment, Katsuragi-kun.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.660
What are your thoughts, gentlemen?

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.380
We can tell he's not an ordinary pitcher, but...

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.360
Yes, that's right.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:58.530
From the VTR, his fastballs are indeed fast.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:04.880
However, on top of not having any good breaking balls, his control is erratic.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:11.030
If you compare him to Mayumura, who's in the same grade and has strong abilities, he's not that great.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.380
W-What are you saying?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.740
Isn't it amazing that he was able to defeat Kawakami Jitsugyo with a complete-game, no-hit shutout using only fastballs!?

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.440
Those fastballs I saw with my own eyes are the real thing!

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.050
And it's not just that! 

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.920
The aura that surrounds him...

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.530
and his presence that seems to overwhelm the opponent...!

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.490
That's too vague.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:35.510
You're ten years too early to be making judgments based on your intuition and feelings, Katsuragi-kun.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.860
To begin with, the fact that he's Honda's son is a big problem.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.730
W-What?

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.930
Honda's death ten years ago was no accident.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.970
It was our team's fault for not having him get a full checkup at the doctor's after he got hit.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.950
That's what everyone thinks.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:04.150
If we go get Honda Junior, it'll suggest that we're trying to use him to create headlines, which'll give us a bad image.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.000
Well then, getting Shigeno is...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.300
Impossible. Besides, the players we're going to nominate this year have already been decided.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:15.710
No way...

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.560
It's annoying, isn't it?

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.710
Chief Yoneda!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.350
If the higher-ups are like that, we won't be able to act on our own.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.380
When you go ahead with your own decision,

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:38.240
there's a big chance that it'll be all for nothing.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.650
Y-Yeah...

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:45.560
However, if you're going to give up after this, you should quit being a scout.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.290
Huh?

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.980
Katsuragi, believe in your intuition.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.510
If you don't believe in your own eyes, you won't be able to do this job.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.470
You should scout the players that you like with heartfelt sincerity.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:01.760
Things such as the team's policy should take a backseat.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:06.350
Anyone who uses money and special treatment as a weapon can be a scout.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.810
Yoneda-san...

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.930
He's a good player.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.050
If you're going to give up, do you want me to do it?

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.490
N-No, I'll do it!

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:21.280
With my own hands, I'll bring Shigeno to our team for sure!

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.750
Did you see it? This morning's sports newspaper?

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.210
Yeah, I saw it, I saw it!

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.370
I guess that a complete-game, no-hit shutout is really amazing.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.800
And it was with that foot of his!

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.330
He rested it during the first and second games,

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.700
so it seems his foot's condition was better than I thought.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.260
Excuse me!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.430
You guys are part of the baseball team, right?

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.670
Y-Yes...

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.720
Is Shigeno-kun here? 

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.690
I'd like his permission to do an interview.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.120
An interview?

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.130
Amazing!

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.480
He's famous!

00:06:54.880 --> 00:07:00.700
If you're looking for Shigeno-senpai, he went with Tashiro-senpai to go check out our next opponent's game.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.820
What? He's not here?

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.650
This is bad...

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.660
Shigeno really is amazing.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.830
Kuriyama against Seikai Dai Fuzoku, huh?

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:18.850
If we look at the results up till now,
then Kuriyama should be our next opponent.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.370
Whoever wins, it's the same, isn't it?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.350
After one more game, we'll be able to go up against Kaido.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.220
As if we could lose at a place like this.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.430
Didn't you actually want to watch Kaido's game?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.440
I'm not in the mood to check it out.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.180
<i>Really? I didn't know. </i>

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.000
<i>You've been doing your best. </i>

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.360
Next time, when I see their faces,

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.700
I'll throw down a challenge to their snobbily held-up noses.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.130
Incredible!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.640
<i>Sato-senpai did?</i>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:13.520
<i>Yeah, it seems as though the royal Kaido-sama doesn't consider Seishuu an opponent.</i>

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.140
<i>That's a lie.</i>

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.720
<i>Sato-senpai wouldn't say such a thing.</i>

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.910
<i>You know what?</i>

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.590
<i>He looked straight at me and said it!</i>

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.030
<i>Because they won the national tournament in the past, they've become arrogant.</i>

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:31.750
<i>Well, if they take it that easy around us, it makes it easier for us to beat them up.</i>

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.130
<i>Sato-senpai is not that kind of person!</i>

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.410
Game over!

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.090
That was so easy, it wasn't even a warmup.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:04.530
In the district tournament, my knuckle is too big of a hurdle.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:08.330
But... your fastballs were getting hit a lot.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.240
Shut up.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:10.950
Huh?

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:13.140
U-Um...

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:13.910
U-Um...

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.360
Hey, hey, who is this?

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.010
Letting the audience in all the way here...

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.000
Go home, go home!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.750
Sato-senpai is...

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.720
Um, I am his kouhai from junior high!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.570
Hey, Sato.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.470
Yeah?

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.520
Ayane-chan.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.960
Um, congratulations on your win in the third game.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.070
Thank you. 

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.580
Did you come watch by yourself?

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.590
Y-Yes!

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.110
I... 

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.920
want to ask you something, senpai!

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:52.450
Toshiya-kun!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:54.030
Long time no see!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:54.910
Ryoko-chan!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.760
I'm so glad I was able to see your game live, Toshiya-kun!

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.080
During the spring tournament...

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.650
I was cheering for you while watching you on television the entire time!

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.540
<i>I wonder who she is...</i>

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:05.840
<i>She's beautiful...</i>

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.430
Did I interrupt you?

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.460
N-No!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:15.100
I'm Sato-senpai's kouhai... Suzuki Ayane.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.180
I'm Kawase Ryoko. Pleased to meet you.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:22.470
Ryoko-chan and I formed a battery during Little League.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:27.580
Right now, she's the Ooiso Kokusai Daigaku's baseball team's female ace.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.700
The mass media's watching her.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.580
I have to get to the point where I'm recognized due to my skill.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.420
I'm finally able to throw a slider,

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.750
so I'm planning to concentrate on the forkball next.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.880
If I don't concentrate on a variety of pitches, I won't be able to defeat the boys since my speed is lacking.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.540
You haven't changed at all. 

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.110
But you surprised me;

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.510
why are you here today?

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:52.950
Yeah, when I saw this, it was a bit nostalgic.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.600
Toshiya-kun, did you see it?

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.290
This sports newspaper!

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.690
Shigeno Goro: complete-game, no-hit shutout!

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.900
Yeah, it was a pretty big spread.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:06.740
Oh, she's the manager for Goro-kun's team.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.330
What? Really!?

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:09.390
Yes.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:12.820
If it's Goro-kun's pitching, that kind of result is to be expected.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:18.300
I was worried about his injury, but it seems as though there's not much of a problem.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.210
I'm so glad...

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:26.460
Shigeno-senpai was saying that Sato-senpai didn't know he was going to be going up against us.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:29.970
That's why I told him there was no way that was true.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:36.060
I'm sure he heard it wrong, because to Sato-senpai, Shigeno-senpai is special-

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.280
It's not a mistake.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:43.030
I've never thought about the match-ups for the district tournament,

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:47.320
because we've practiced enough to defeat any team at any time.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:56.030
So the number one team is full of confidence.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.880
But I wonder if it'll go according to plan.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.120
Your opponent is Goro-kun.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:06.500
At that time too, we were a team that was supposed to win.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:13.090
His baseball sense and tenacity was what upset our victory, wasn't it?

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:19.120
I know his skill level better than anyone.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.070
That's why I can say that.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.350
He won't be able to defeat us now.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.570
B-But...

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.260
aren't you looking forward to your match with Shigeno-senpai?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:32.900
Because we have no way of practicing against a 150km/h fastball,

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.370
if we can get some practice with him,

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.920
it'll be a useful exercise before Koshien.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.900
Hey, Sato! The bus is leaving!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.160
I'll be right there.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:47.770
See you later.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:48.750
Yeah.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:49.750
That's right.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:52.090
Ayane-chan, you had something that you wanted to talk to me about?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.090
No, it's fine now.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:00.860
I'm sorry.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.600
You had to talk to Toshiya-kun about something, right?

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:04.770
No!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.250
I'm looking forward to it.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:11.400
If it's Goro-kun, I'm sure he'll do something.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.690
If there's anything I can do, let me know, okay?

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.860
Bye!

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:26.120
Those guys...

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:31.050
<i>They've gotten this much stronger!</i>

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:37.050
This is a free fansub.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:37.050
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.770
<i>Kuriyama's ace, Katori, and the cleanup batter, Karasawa.</i>

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.400
<i>Even at the Kaido entrance exam... </i>

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.850
<i>their skills were amazing.</i>

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:55.830
<i>If Toshi hadn't hit a home run,</i>

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.330
<i>I don't know if we'd have been able to win.</i>

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.520
<i>The problem is Katori's high-speed slider.</i>

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.080
<i>It's not a pitch that our batters will be able to hit.</i>

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:14.130
<i>I guess I'll have to hit it.</i>

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:17.170
A 140km/h high-speed slider!?

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.620
That's impossible.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.510
There's no batting center that would have that kind of machine.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:25.720
Damn!

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:28.940
And there's only three days left till the game!

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.990
Shigeno Goro-kun, right?

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:41.190
Wait a sec.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.680
Sorry, but if it's an interview, I refuse.

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:46.660
Ever since I appeared in the newspaper, it's been annoying.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:47.700
See ya.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:49.920
I'm not part of the mass media.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:54.960
Nice to meet you.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:59.860
I'm a scout for the Yokohama Blue Oceans, Katsuragi.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:00.730
And?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.770
For a high school student at this time...

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:07.150
Isn't it against the rules for a pro scout to try to contact us?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:10.600
If people see this, I'm the one who's going to be in trouble.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:14.790
W-Well, if it's just this, then it's not a problem.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:19.360
If someone asks about it, you could just say that some old man stopped to ask you for directions.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:23.040
I just went to meet with your parents.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:28.020
I've been friends with your father for a long time.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:30.230
I asked him straight out...

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:34.860
if you wanted to become a pro after you graduate from high school.

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:37.710
However, the answer was short.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.670
It was "I don't know. Ask him yourself."

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.990
To that kind of question, it's the same answer, even if you ask me.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.430
I'm thinking a lot about my next game.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.310
I see.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.770
Well, if you could just remember my face for today...

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.780
I won't remember it.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.530
<i>Not becoming a pro, but the game in front of him, huh?</i>

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.450
<i>I see. He really is their son.</i>

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:05.680
Oh, that's right...

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:14.930
Then here I go.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:19.800
I-It turned!

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:21.630
Are you serious?

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:29.490
They say it's an old technique they can't use anymore.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.180
Some strange old man told me.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.560
Old man? Who?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:39.320
<i>A pro can't help with a high schooler's baseball practice,</i>

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:43.530
<i>but I know a way for you to be able to practice hitting sliders. </i>

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:48.690
But unless we can get someone who has a fast fastball to throw,

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:52.380
it won't be practice for that high-speed slider.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:55.040
If you practice hitting, who's going to pitch?

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.960
I'm the only one who can do it.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:00.810
What?

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:02.130
But you... Your finger...

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:05.040
There're only three days left!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.970
There's no time to think about it!

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.180
Taiga.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.140
Here I go!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.920
Hey, Taiga, are you all right?

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:25.070
If you're going to worry about me, then just hurry up and hit it.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.240
All right, come!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:35.760
H-Hey!

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:36.710
We have to practice too!

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.630
Y-Yeah!

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:45.580
Ayane-chan, 

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.430
are you feeling a bit better?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.990
<i>He won't be able to defeat us now.</i>

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:57.830
<i>It annoyed me.</i>

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:02.010
<i>I guess I am a member of Seishuu's baseball team!</i>

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:10.990
Nakamura-senpai.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.240
I love this team!

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.790
Taiga!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.250
Just stop, Taiga!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.670
You shouldn't continue anymore!

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:30.310
How pathetic.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.350
I've only thrown about 20 or 30 pitches.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:35.560
Thanks to you, I'm slowly getting the timing down.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.100
Let's end here for today.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.140
But...

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.860
<i>I'm finally able to throw a slider.</i>

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:53.530
<i>If there's anything I can do, let me know, okay?</i>

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:55.540
Um, please excuse me.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:58.480
I'm going to leave early today!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.500
Ayane-chan?

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.150
This year's Kuriyama is good.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:19.320
Their hitting and fielding are all pretty good.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:23.100
Their ace, Katori, hasn't allowed any earned runs in three games.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:27.230
It'll be an interesting game between the pitchers when they play against complete-game, no-hit shutout Shigeno.

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:32.570
Yes, because they probably won't be able to hit Shigeno's 150km/h fastball that easily.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.570
All right.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.410
Time for free batting.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.970
Set the machine for Karasawa mode.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.540
Karasawa mode?

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:44.500
All right. 130km/h.

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:47.710
140km/h.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.760
145km/h.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:54.640
150km/h.

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:03.980
I-It doesn't seem as though it'll be a pitchers' game.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:18.540
You bastard!

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.000
Do you have something against me or something!?

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.830
Huh? That's strange...

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.390
Are you sure you don't want me to pitch?

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:26.800
You can't!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.180
All right.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.180
My shoulders are finally starting to warm up.

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.980
I'm going to start getting serious.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.900
Hey, Tashiro, can't you pitch?

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.000
That's right...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:36.930
Hey!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.220
Good morning.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:41.100
Good morning.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:44.640
Ayane-chan, who is that person?

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.900
Long time no see, Goro-kun.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.830
R-Ryoko-chan!

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.030
Why are you here?

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.970
Because I want you to go up against Kaido, Goro-kun.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:08.590
I'll help you out with your slider practice.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:10.450
I-It's a girl.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.050
And she's gorgeous.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:14.510
What kind of relationship does she have with Shigeno?

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:18.900
I'm thankful you're willing to help, but I don't get it.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:21.650
You were former teammates with Toshiya.

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:24.810
I'm determined to defeat Kaido, you know?

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:27.020
You have to be.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:31.280
It seems like fun to defeat Kaido,

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:34.990
which is considered the best team in high school baseball.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:39.740
Then, here I go!

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:41.120
Y-Yeah!

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:52.980
Well?

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:54.340
Will you be able to practice?

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:11.830
Amazing.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:15.200
100 in the morning, and 200 after school!

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.200
Do those guys have monstrous amounts of stamina or what!?

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:33.300
I'm getting to the point where I can see it now.

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:34.930
You've done well.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:36.440
But...

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.920
I won't let you hit it easily!

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:41.900
So you still hate to lose.

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.010
That's exactly what I'm looking for.

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.550
More, more! 

00:23:00.550 --> 00:23:01.990
I'm going to keep going!

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:03.680
This is exactly what I'm looking for!

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:06.480
<i>We won't lose, Sato-senpai!</i>

00:24:40.710 --> 00:24:42.590
The Kuriyama game begins!

00:24:42.590 --> 00:24:44.780
I'll show them the results of my special training!

00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:45.480
But...

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:47.430
they know we're aiming for the slider!

00:24:48.130 --> 00:24:50.640
We can't allow them to get any runs!

00:24:52.450 --> 00:24:53.840
Next time, on Major: 

00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:54.900
Pitchers' Duel!

00:24:55.290 --> 00:24:57.790
Run to the stage of your dreams!
